cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Segment Graphs and Language Models for Music Context Understanding:
  A Multi-Task Study with Explicit Leakage Accounting
message: If you use this software or its findings, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Utsha
    family-names: Basak
    email: utsha23basak@gmail.com
    affiliation: BRAC University
  - given-names: Mohammad Tanvir
    family-names: Hossain
    affiliation: BRAC University
  - given-names: Nabil
    family-names: Mahmud
    affiliation: BRAC University
repository-code: https://github.com/UtshaBasak/GNN-BERT-Music-Context-Understanding
abstract: >-
  A hybrid BERT and graph neural network system for music context
  understanding. Each track is represented as a segment graph whose nodes carry
  a fixed 96-dimensional descriptor and whose edges combine a temporal chain
  with k-nearest-neighbour similarity links. One representation supports four
  tasks: text-only tagging, graph-only genre classification, cross-attention
  fusion with multi-task emotion regression, and contrastive graph-caption
  retrieval, across four public corpora totalling 35,984 tracks. The study
  quantifies three sources of optimistic bias that are usually inherited rather
  than measured: caption-to-label leakage on MusicCaps worth 0.1963 macro-F1,
  a MagnaTagATune split that is not artist-disjoint, and test-split information
  entering the label vocabulary through corpus-wide frequency selection.
keywords:
  - music information retrieval
  - graph neural networks
  - multi-task learning
  - label leakage
  - automatic tagging
  - cross-modal retrieval
license: MIT
